{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc, a large jump over the single-profile multimodal baseline (config_016, 0.527). However, this comparison conflates three changes: adding a second modality (already tested), switching to multiprofile, and introducing avgpool aggregation. The critical open question is whether the multiprofile+avgpool benefit is inherent to the RNA representation or requires the multimodal interaction. config_002 (RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA n2000, avgpool) is a clean single-variable extension of config_001 (RNA-only, single-profile) that isolates the multiprofile/aggregation effect on the RNA side alone. If RNA multiprofile alone yields a substantial gain (e.g., >0.55), the benefit is in the RNA profile representation and we should prioritize multiprofile RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) next. If it stays near 0.485, the gain is synergistic and we should focus on the multimodal aggregation design (e.g., transformer in config_020). This ablation is the highest-information experiment under the budget because it disambiguates the mechanism behind the largest observed effect and directly guides the next 2-3 experiments."
}

